                <pb facs="0787" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-16T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1919,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your despatch No. 2720 of May 9.</p>
                <p>Department does not consider that you should undertake to extend protection to
                    nationals of non-treaty countries unless requested by those Governments,
                    consented to by China and authorized by Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
